# B0 (no card opened): build the window image tp4-w2-1 from the pushed tp4/w2 commit. It runs FIRST, before the card-M jobs, because those run in this image (see ORDER.txt); building opens no
# card, so no quad job holds the cards and the card-M-before-quad rule stands. The profile named is the production default; nothing is baked as the image default (no C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE).
# THE TAG MUST BE FRESH: the build step skips a tag that already exists. THREE NEW SERVED FILES (gdn_conv_gates_spread.py and its reader and writer kernels, F1) and the multi-user SDPA modules of tp4/sdpa-multi are in both image copy lists and the overlay.
# READ: the build log's provenance report with no problem line, the closure checks pass, the image id printed. Never run it during a timing job. Duration (estimate): 20-60 min. Stop rule: a build or provenance failure stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/w2 eight-seat 262k wave-2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/w2 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
